<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>MagSafe</strong> - Even though foldable iPhone dummies we saw earlier this year <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/24/iphone-ultra-could-be-missing-5-features/">didn't have a MagSafe ring</a>, <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a> claims all signs indicate <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/01/foldable-iphone-ultra-magsafe/">MagSafe charging will be supported</a>.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Crease</strong> - Some of the early language about the foldable iPhone's crease suggested Apple might have found a way <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/02/25/apple-2026-foldable-phone-has-no-crease/">to make it invisible</a>, but later rumors are more realistic. The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/02/25/iphone-fold-crease-measured-production/">crease is minimal</a>, but Apple hasn't found a magic way to get rid of it.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Touch ID</strong> - <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/touch-id/">Touch ID</a> is still expected for the foldable iPhone. Apple didn't have room for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mask-face-id/">Face ID</a> hardware because the device is rumored to be just 4.5mm thick. There will be volume buttons at the top of the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/iphone-ultra/">iPhone Ultra</a>, with a &zwnj;Touch ID&zwnj; side button for unlocking.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Software</strong> - <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/08/ios-27-hints-at-foldable-iphone-with-app-resizability-push/">makes it clear</a> Apple is making sure apps will work with the foldable iPhone. There's a big push for app resizability and layout flexibility. The iPhone is expected to support multitasking, sidebars, and side-by-side app usage.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Cameras</strong> - Camera rumors haven't changed. We're expecting a two-lens camera setup with Wide and Ultra Wide lenses.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Chips</strong> - Early rumors said Apple would transition to the C2 and move away from Qualcomm, but it looks like Apple might still use Qualcomm modems <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/02/iphone-18-pro-could-use-qualcomm-modem-in-the-us/">in the United States</a>. It hinges on whether the C2 supports mmWave 5G. The &zwnj;iPhone Ultra&zwnj; will also adopt Apple's A20 Pro chip, the same as the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> models.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Colors</strong> - The foldable iPhone is expected in white/silver and dark blue.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Apple Pencil</strong> - Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/30/apple-pencil-for-iphone-ultra-was-tested/">tested an Apple Pencil</a> with the foldable iPhone, but it's probably not going to launch.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Launch Timing</strong> - Rumors on &zwnj;iPhone Ultra&zwnj; launch timing and production have been mixed, with some sources reporting delays. Gurman says he will be "very surprised" if the device doesn't launch at the same time as the &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; models or "very close to it." It's still possible supplies could be constrained, leading to long waits for those who don't pre-order early.</li><br/>
